# Confirm when the ask is ambiguous across journal options

If the latest message can mean **more than one named scheme** in
`journals/` or the CLI (option 1 vs 2, strat vs fixedstim, Harris vs
shuffle, split vs unsplit, true / act / bayes prior, …), **stop and
ask** before implementing or submitting jobs. Do not pick the reading
that is easiest to wire.

## This repo (incident 2026-08-22)

“Within each shuffle stratum” + fitted AK + copy-last was implemented
as **option 2 (`fixedstim`)** — real stim, labels at real `elig_idx`.
The user meant **option 1 (`strat`)** — new pseudo-session, remake
stim×act-prior (choice) or stim×choice (act_block) on that draw.
A full BWM FDR was run on the wrong arm.

Journal source of truth: [structured_nulls_choice_lr.md](journals/structured_nulls_choice_lr.md)
(option 1 = `_pseudo_strat`, option 2 = `_pseudo_fixed`).

## What to do

1. Name the candidate options in the user’s words (e.g. “option 1
   stratified pseudo” vs “option 2 fixed real stim”).
2. Ask which one. Do not submit ORCD / write the arm until they pick.
3. After they pick, implement **only** that one.

Do not treat “same stratum as shuffle” as approval for `fixedstim`.
Option 1 remakes that stratum **on the pseudo**.
